###### WIKIPEDIA

#### =E2=9D=8C** **[_**Wikipedia bans AI from writing its articles**_](http=
s://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Writing_articles_with_large_language_mo=
dels)

View image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=3Dscale-down,forma=
t=3Dauto,onerror=3Dredirect,quality=3D80/uploads/asset/file/0aeba1aa-e1b9-4=
c45-84fa-61ed139cb103/wikipediaban.jpg?t=3D1774560673)
Caption: Image source: Wikipedia

**The Rundown: **Wikipedia's volunteer editors [banned](https://en.wikipedi=
a.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Writing_articles_with_large_language_models) the use o=
f AI to write articles on the foundation=E2=80=99s English-language site, a=
 move the policy's author called a "pushback against enshittification and f=
orceful push of AI by so many companies=E2=80=9D.=20

**The details: **

* Prior attempts at broad AI rules failed to reach consensus, but mounting =
AI-generated errors pushed editors to a near-unanimous 40-2 vote.

* The ban covers writing or rewriting articles with LLMs, with editors stil=
l allowed to use AI for grammar fixes and translations with human review.

* The policy's author [said](https://wikis.world/@quarknova/116262752178419=
633) the change could "spark a broader change" and "empower communities on =
other platforms" to set AI rules on their own terms.

* StackOverflow and German Wikipedia  have enacted similar bans, with Spani=
sh Wikipedia going further to fully ban the use of AI, even for editing pur=
poses.=20

**Why it matters: **AI text reportedly [surpassed](https://x.com/wintonARK/=
status/2037208130703286457?s=3D20) human output for the first time in 2025,=
 and Wikipedia is trying to hold the human line, all while Elon pushes Grok=
ipedia (an AI-created version of Wikipedia) in the exact opposite direction=
. The internet's most-used knowledge base bet against the current, but how =
long that holds is anyone=E2=80=99s guess.


